1
00:01:41,950 --> 00:01:49,009
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,430 --> 00:01:51,930
[Episode 5]

3
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:04,560
I told myself,

4
00:02:07,140 --> 00:02:08,600
it's great to have a rival.

5
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:11,820
Whether I win or lose,
all is fair and square.

6
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,900
But another voice in my heart

7
00:02:15,530 --> 00:02:16,630
keeps asking.

8
00:02:18,870 --> 00:02:21,600
It was you who held my hand
to escape the aquarium.

9
00:02:22,710 --> 00:02:24,970
It was you who buried
the wish box with me.

10
00:02:28,430 --> 00:02:29,860
If this isn't a friend,

11
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:33,360
then what should a friend be like?

12
00:03:00,410 --> 00:03:00,960
Hey—

13
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:05,840
Lin Zhixia!

14
00:03:06,310 --> 00:03:07,970
Why are you so absent-minded?

15
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:12,960
What's wrong?

16
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:14,840
The only person in our group
who can't have any problems

17
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:15,740
is you.

18
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:17,710
Otherwise, as someone
tagging along for the contest,

19
00:03:17,710 --> 00:03:19,770
I won't be able to explain it to my mom.

20
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:27,690
I...

21
00:03:30,150 --> 00:03:31,520
I have a friend.

22
00:03:33,590 --> 00:03:35,120
Don't say "friend." I know.

23
00:03:35,190 --> 00:03:36,190
Just say it's you.

24
00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:37,850
I really have a friend.

25
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:43,079
He's quite nice to me,

26
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,960
and I've always treated him
as a good friend.

27
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:47,560
But recently I heard them say

28
00:03:49,590 --> 00:03:50,800
that they only sees me as a rival

29
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:52,060
and wants to defeat me.

30
00:03:53,410 --> 00:03:55,000
I've seen plenty of girls like this.

31
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,260
Don't take it to heart.

32
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:58,560
He's a boy.

33
00:03:59,870 --> 00:04:01,470
A boy is acting like that too?

34
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:07,410
Lin Zhixia, I didn't know you well before.

35
00:04:07,630 --> 00:04:08,630
I thought you

36
00:04:08,650 --> 00:04:11,080
disdained hanging out
with us ordinary people.

37
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,360
But in this period of time,

38
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:14,290
I felt you're actually quite nice.

39
00:04:14,370 --> 00:04:17,170
You just aren't good at
getting along with people.

40
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:19,110
Listen to me.

41
00:04:19,829 --> 00:04:22,160
This friend is definitely jealous of you.

42
00:04:22,430 --> 00:04:23,760
He treats me quite well.

43
00:04:25,430 --> 00:04:26,270
Then...

44
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:30,070
did he ask you to tutor him

45
00:04:30,570 --> 00:04:32,110
or ask what books you read

46
00:04:32,110 --> 00:04:34,040
and what practice questions you do?

47
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,330
See, he's just using you.

48
00:04:35,330 --> 00:04:36,920
That's why he treats you well.

49
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:37,830
Listen to me.

50
00:04:37,830 --> 00:04:39,490
I'm very experienced in this.

51
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:41,120
But...

52
00:04:41,140 --> 00:04:42,409
Fine,

53
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:43,800
if you don't believe me,

54
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:45,200
don't you believe books?

55
00:04:45,370 --> 00:04:47,360
I remember a good quote from a book.

56
00:04:47,510 --> 00:04:49,630
Time will filter out fake friends.

57
00:04:49,830 --> 00:04:50,480
This friend of yours

58
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:52,190
is a fake friend filtered out by time.

59
00:04:52,190 --> 00:04:53,120
Just ignore him.

60
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:58,130
Then I should just
give him the cold shoulder?

61
00:04:59,190 --> 00:05:01,000
Time will give you the answer.

62
00:05:07,950 --> 00:05:08,920
It's about time.

63
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:10,320
Let's go back and review.

64
00:05:11,870 --> 00:05:13,670
I thought we were done for today.

65
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,360
Okay, let's do some practice.

66
00:05:51,990 --> 00:05:54,640
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

67
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:53,600
Now, open your book.

68
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:55,310
Turn to page 27.

69
00:05:58,770 --> 00:05:59,700
Comprehending:

70
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:00,310
one.

71
00:06:00,930 --> 00:06:02,300
Read the passage carefully

72
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:04,980
and join the correct part
of the sentences.

73
00:06:28,450 --> 00:06:29,330
Lin Zhixia.

74
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,500
You caused me to miss the contest.

75
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:37,220
But you prepared
quite well yourself, didn't you?

76
00:06:39,130 --> 00:06:40,260
Wh-What do you want?

77
00:06:40,930 --> 00:06:41,810
Nothing.

78
00:06:42,570 --> 00:06:44,220
I'm free now anyway.

79
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:45,980
I have plenty of time.

80
00:06:54,370 --> 00:06:55,980
You don't think you can just stick up

81
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:57,100
for Duan Qiyan

82
00:06:57,310 --> 00:06:58,770
and then walk away, do you?

83
00:07:00,770 --> 00:07:01,830
What are you doing?

84
00:07:06,570 --> 00:07:08,540
If I see you approach Lin Zhixia again,

85
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:11,180
it won't be as simple as
withdrawing from the contest.

86
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,640
Do you want to be expelled?

87
00:07:15,660 --> 00:07:16,450
Lin Zhixia,

88
00:07:17,740 --> 00:07:19,330
I'll say it right here.

89
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:20,860
Tomorrow,

90
00:07:21,750 --> 00:07:25,210
don't even think about
participating in the contest in peace.

91
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:27,330
Let's wait and see.

92
00:07:34,930 --> 00:07:35,740
Are you okay?

93
00:08:00,330 --> 00:08:01,130
Zeqiu,

94
00:08:01,810 --> 00:08:03,870
I want to talk to you about something.

95
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:08,300
Can you...

96
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:09,570
No.

97
00:08:11,770 --> 00:08:13,100
I'm trying to say—can you

98
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:14,760
go to school with me tomorrow?

99
00:08:15,930 --> 00:08:16,920
Did I tell you that at school,

100
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:18,330
you're not allowed to mention
that you're my sister?

101
00:08:18,330 --> 00:08:19,620
You did, but...

102
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:20,620
Since you're not my sister,

103
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:21,860
how can I accompany you to school?

104
00:08:21,860 --> 00:08:23,790
It will cause misunderstandings.

105
00:08:25,570 --> 00:08:27,370
Just for tomorrow, please?

106
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:29,660
Just one day.

107
00:08:33,270 --> 00:08:34,530
Did something happen?

108
00:08:36,510 --> 00:08:37,030
No.

109
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:38,150
Nothing.

110
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:46,320
Keep a distance of 10 meters.

111
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:47,580
What?

112
00:08:48,860 --> 00:08:50,510
I mean,
when we go to school together tomorrow,

113
00:08:50,510 --> 00:08:52,110
keep a distance of 10 meters.

114
00:08:52,650 --> 00:08:53,580
Don't talk to me,

115
00:08:53,630 --> 00:08:54,770
and no eye contact.

116
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:56,800
Don't let others misunderstand.

117
00:08:57,580 --> 00:08:59,380
And when we enter the door later,

118
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:01,390
you only enter when I say so.

119
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:03,100
Okay.

120
00:09:05,250 --> 00:09:06,310
Good night, Zeqiu.

121
00:09:06,410 --> 00:09:07,070
Good night.

122
00:10:40,770 --> 00:10:41,770
Two more minutes.

123
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:42,770
If time is up

124
00:10:42,770 --> 00:10:44,030
and your team isn't all here,

125
00:10:44,030 --> 00:10:44,890
you can't participate.

126
00:10:44,380 --> 00:10:48,630
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

127
00:10:51,290 --> 00:10:52,490
Where is Jiang Yubai?

128
00:10:53,250 --> 00:10:54,380
I don't know either.

129
00:11:22,650 --> 00:11:25,520
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

130
00:11:33,340 --> 00:11:33,980
I'm here!

131
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:35,610
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

132
00:11:38,620 --> 00:11:39,250
Sit down.

133
00:11:42,860 --> 00:11:45,730
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

134
00:11:53,470 --> 00:11:55,470
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

135
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:11,650
The test is out of 100 points.

136
00:12:11,860 --> 00:12:13,500
You have 120 minutes.

137
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:15,740
You may begin now.

138
00:12:15,470 --> 00:12:16,950
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

139
00:12:24,250 --> 00:12:26,760
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

140
00:12:48,430 --> 00:12:49,930
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

141
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:54,750
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

142
00:13:28,860 --> 00:13:29,650
Lin Zhixia,

143
00:13:31,170 --> 00:13:32,410
that multiple-choice question,

144
00:13:32,410 --> 00:13:33,340
the last one,

145
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:34,910
where xy > 0

146
00:13:35,170 --> 00:13:36,770
and x+y = 1,

147
00:13:36,770 --> 00:13:37,700
do you remember?

148
00:13:39,410 --> 00:13:40,740
Is the answer C?

149
00:13:41,050 --> 00:13:41,460
A.

150
00:13:42,650 --> 00:13:45,250
By introducing auxiliary variables through
variable relationship transformations

151
00:13:45,250 --> 00:13:46,740
and then applying
the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,

152
00:13:46,740 --> 00:13:48,870
the minimum value
can be solved as 1/3.

153
00:13:52,250 --> 00:13:55,770
We talked about a similar question
in the library the day before yesterday.

154
00:13:55,770 --> 00:13:57,130
I'm doomed.

155
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:02,820
I saw you sleep for 15 minutes
in the second half.

156
00:14:02,820 --> 00:14:04,950
You completed it so quickly this time.

157
00:14:04,980 --> 00:14:06,240
Speed doesn't matter.

158
00:14:06,340 --> 00:14:07,170
The last question

159
00:14:07,170 --> 00:14:08,890
was obviously out of my league.

160
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:10,050
If you ask a dog

161
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:11,820
to answer a Chinese test question,

162
00:14:11,820 --> 00:14:13,010
could it answer it?

163
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:14,050
That's how I felt.

164
00:14:14,050 --> 00:14:15,510
You seem quite proud of it.

165
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:17,070
I might not get first place,

166
00:14:17,070 --> 00:14:19,400
but I definitely won't drag our team down.

167
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:24,540
I told you that you shouldn't have
chosen me as a teammate.

168
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:26,940
Ms. Last In Class.

169
00:14:27,370 --> 00:14:28,700
How did you do this time?

170
00:14:29,370 --> 00:14:30,900
It's none of your business.

171
00:14:31,290 --> 00:14:32,100
Ignore him.

172
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:36,050
Let's go. Let's find a place
to help you estimate your score.

173
00:14:36,050 --> 00:14:36,860
The library?

174
00:14:37,770 --> 00:14:38,980
The library again?

175
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:40,130
I'm hungry.

176
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:42,430
We can eat first.

177
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:43,740
Let's go.

178
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:45,530
Lin Zhixia.

179
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:49,290
Don't worry.

180
00:14:49,820 --> 00:14:51,750
Your team will definitely make it.

181
00:14:53,530 --> 00:14:55,530
I'll compete with you in the finals.

182
00:14:57,220 --> 00:14:58,020
Rest assured.

183
00:14:58,250 --> 00:14:59,050
This time,

184
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:01,560
I'll let you know me more completely.

185
00:15:09,980 --> 00:15:10,740
I'm doomed.

186
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:13,180
I can't even remember if I wrote my name.

187
00:15:17,770 --> 00:15:18,860
Even if I did,

188
00:15:18,860 --> 00:15:20,890
I definitely did terribly on this test.

189
00:15:20,890 --> 00:15:22,220
I might not even pass.

190
00:15:29,940 --> 00:15:31,740
Why did you lose confidence too?

191
00:15:33,250 --> 00:15:36,010
I just talked big to Jiang Yubai.

192
00:15:37,130 --> 00:15:38,740
If we don't make it to the finals,

193
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:40,220
won't it be super awkward?

194
00:15:40,290 --> 00:15:41,820
What did you just say to him?

195
00:15:42,010 --> 00:15:44,370
"I'll let you know me more completely."

196
00:15:44,770 --> 00:15:45,580
I think

197
00:15:46,530 --> 00:15:48,460
it was even more arrogant than that.

198
00:15:48,460 --> 00:15:50,050
I also told him before

199
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:52,590
that until the finals are over,

200
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:54,530
I'd unfriend him

201
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:56,800
for this to be a pure competition.

202
00:15:57,940 --> 00:15:59,290
You really hyped it up.

203
00:16:02,890 --> 00:16:03,890
Sorry, sorry.

204
00:16:04,370 --> 00:16:05,290
It's all my fault.

205
00:16:05,290 --> 00:16:06,690
This is so embarrassing.

206
00:16:14,910 --> 00:16:16,530
Anyway, the exam is over.

207
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:18,130
Whether we make it or not,

208
00:16:18,130 --> 00:16:19,720
the result can't be changed.

209
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:21,690
Let's just have a happy dinner tonight.

210
00:16:21,690 --> 00:16:22,820
Don't overthink it.

211
00:16:23,100 --> 00:16:23,890
My treat.

212
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:28,900
Screwing up the exam,

213
00:16:29,170 --> 00:16:30,770
even the skewers don't taste good anymore.

214
00:16:30,770 --> 00:16:32,570
Who said you screwed up the exam?

215
00:16:32,890 --> 00:16:35,370
You can't keep giving yourself
this kind of psychological suggestion.

216
00:16:35,370 --> 00:16:37,230
Do you know the Law of Attraction?

217
00:16:37,820 --> 00:16:38,700
What's that?

218
00:16:39,250 --> 00:16:40,910
It's a psychological effect.

219
00:16:41,130 --> 00:16:42,700
If you always think about bad things,

220
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:44,530
your life will be full of crises.

221
00:16:44,890 --> 00:16:47,410
If you always focus on the good things,

222
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:49,240
you'll attract good results.

223
00:16:50,010 --> 00:16:50,890
How?

224
00:16:51,130 --> 00:16:53,660
Your thoughts and emotions
emit a frequency.

225
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:54,620
This frequency

226
00:16:54,620 --> 00:16:57,410
can attract things
with the same frequency in the universe.

227
00:16:57,410 --> 00:17:00,010
So you have to
place an order with the universe.

228
00:17:01,050 --> 00:17:02,250
That sounds amazing.

229
00:17:02,770 --> 00:17:04,420
All right, let's place an order now.

230
00:17:03,690 --> 00:17:04,579
[Three-Two Kitchen]

231
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:05,099
Come on.

232
00:17:06,609 --> 00:17:07,069
Come on.

233
00:17:11,260 --> 00:17:13,900
We will definitely
do very well in the exam this time,

234
00:17:13,900 --> 00:17:15,290
and we will definitely advance.

235
00:17:15,290 --> 00:17:17,810
We will definitely
do very well in the exam this time,

236
00:17:17,810 --> 00:17:19,050
and we will definitely advance.

237
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:19,880
[Three-Two Kitchen]

238
00:17:19,140 --> 00:17:22,400
Tang Tingting definitely
wrote her name on the test paper.

239
00:17:22,849 --> 00:17:26,089
Tang Tingting definitely
wrote her name on the test paper.

240
00:17:26,089 --> 00:17:27,900
Then I hope my two friends

241
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:28,900
won't be so depressed tonight,

242
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:30,960
and we can have a happy meal together.

243
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:33,010
It seems to really work.

244
00:17:33,050 --> 00:17:35,330
I feel quite happy now.

245
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:36,190
[Three-Two Kitchen]

246
00:17:37,940 --> 00:17:39,570
Do you guys feel

247
00:17:40,290 --> 00:17:42,660
like we used to be just teammates,

248
00:17:43,050 --> 00:17:45,110
but now we're more like good friends?

249
00:17:46,530 --> 00:17:48,610
Actually, in a way,

250
00:17:48,850 --> 00:17:50,660
teammates have a deeper bond than friends.

251
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:53,700
After all, we have to experience success,
failure, joy, and sorrow together.

252
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:56,660
Working together
forces you to adapt to each other

253
00:17:56,660 --> 00:17:58,190
and understand each other.

254
00:17:58,460 --> 00:17:59,460
In difficult times,

255
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:01,720
we will understand and trust each other.

256
00:18:02,530 --> 00:18:04,270
So since we are teammates,

257
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:06,360
we are naturally friends.

258
00:18:08,850 --> 00:18:09,910
Let's make a toast.

259
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:13,180
We will definitely
do very well in the exam this time,

260
00:18:13,180 --> 00:18:14,220
and we will definitely advance.

261
00:18:14,220 --> 00:18:14,950
Definitely!

262
00:18:15,010 --> 00:18:15,980
Cheers!

263
00:18:17,730 --> 00:18:21,550
[Three-Two Kitchen]

264
00:18:21,840 --> 00:18:23,790
[School notice board]

265
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:25,830
Lin Zhixia, look for it quickly.

266
00:18:25,830 --> 00:18:26,960
I don't dare to look.

267
00:18:27,350 --> 00:18:29,200
[Announcement of the Finalists]

268
00:18:28,290 --> 00:18:28,820
Let's go.

269
00:18:33,100 --> 00:18:35,420
What's wrong? Did we not make it?

270
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:38,100
We made it.

271
00:18:38,750 --> 00:18:39,550
Fourth place.

272
00:18:40,570 --> 00:18:41,300
Who is first?

273
00:18:42,090 --> 00:18:43,940
A team from the experimental school.

274
00:18:43,940 --> 00:18:45,850
They won because of their average score.

275
00:18:45,850 --> 00:18:47,580
What about Jiang Yubai's team?

276
00:18:49,660 --> 00:18:51,120
You're thinking about us?

277
00:18:51,570 --> 00:18:52,970
We are not that talented—

278
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:55,830
just the runner-up in the preliminaries.

279
00:19:00,010 --> 00:19:01,070
Congratulations.

