the reassigned tasks.

554
00:33:38,270 --> 00:33:39,070
How about

555
00:33:39,510 --> 00:33:41,270
we find Tang Tingting first?

556
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:47,660
Let her take a break to adjust.

557
00:33:47,920 --> 00:33:49,830
She can join us when she feels better.

558
00:33:49,830 --> 00:33:51,480
She is emotionally unstable right now,

559
00:33:51,480 --> 00:33:53,880
so she's prone
to making mistakes in a rush.

560
00:33:53,880 --> 00:33:55,340
If we want to win 1st place,

561
00:33:55,510 --> 00:33:57,040
we have no margin for error.

562
00:34:01,500 --> 00:34:02,560
Let's do as you say.

563
00:34:06,340 --> 00:34:14,719
[Women]

564
00:34:17,400 --> 00:34:18,400
Ms. Last In Class.

565
00:34:19,230 --> 00:34:22,020
You have the worst score
in the whole competition.

566
00:34:22,020 --> 00:34:26,770
[Women]

567
00:34:23,590 --> 00:34:24,730
You have nothing to lose,

568
00:34:24,730 --> 00:34:26,380
so why not give it your all?

569
00:34:27,150 --> 00:34:29,409
This isn't just about winning or losing.

570
00:34:29,480 --> 00:34:30,230
It's for the 2 teammates

571
00:34:30,230 --> 00:34:32,110
who have always trusted you.

572
00:34:33,800 --> 00:34:35,630
They have never given up on you.

573
00:34:36,670 --> 00:34:37,400
Nor have they ever

574
00:34:37,400 --> 00:34:39,330
treated you as just a benchwarmer.

575
00:34:40,480 --> 00:34:42,110
Instead, they did everything they could,

576
00:34:42,110 --> 00:34:43,630
trying their best to help you

577
00:34:43,630 --> 00:34:44,830
improve your skills.

578
00:34:45,760 --> 00:34:46,630
I'm here.

579
00:34:46,630 --> 00:34:47,360
Don't worry.

580
00:34:47,360 --> 00:34:48,690
Since we are teammates,

581
00:34:49,070 --> 00:34:50,190
we are naturally friends too.

582
00:34:50,190 --> 00:34:52,280
We will definitely
do very well in the exam this time,

583
00:34:52,280 --> 00:34:53,320
and we will definitely advance.

584
00:34:53,320 --> 00:34:54,070
Definitely.

585
00:34:54,070 --> 00:34:55,230
Cheers.

586
00:35:07,280 --> 00:35:08,960
It's also for your mother.

587
00:35:10,440 --> 00:35:11,230
I know.

588
00:35:11,880 --> 00:35:13,400
You must feel embarrassed

589
00:35:13,920 --> 00:35:15,280
because in the whole arena,

590
00:35:15,280 --> 00:35:16,710
only your parent came,

591
00:35:16,710 --> 00:35:19,170
and you even answered
the question wrongly.

592
00:35:19,760 --> 00:35:21,210
But do you know what I saw?

593
00:35:22,320 --> 00:35:23,960
I saw that in your mum's eyes,

594
00:35:24,190 --> 00:35:26,110
she thinks you're a great daughter—

595
00:35:26,110 --> 00:35:28,070
one that's able to stand in
the provincial Math Olympiad arena.

596
00:35:28,070 --> 00:35:29,880
There's no one else in her eyes.

597
00:35:30,760 --> 00:35:32,070
She was using a camera

598
00:35:32,070 --> 00:35:35,800
to record highlights of moments
exclusively yours the whole time.

599
00:35:41,510 --> 00:35:42,320
Of course.

600
00:35:43,880 --> 00:35:45,880
This is also fighting for yourself.

601
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:48,590
Although I usually

602
00:35:48,760 --> 00:35:49,920
call you Ms. Last In Class

603
00:35:49,920 --> 00:35:51,650
and tease you from time to time,

604
00:35:52,920 --> 00:35:55,050
I've really been admiring you lately.

605
00:35:56,360 --> 00:35:58,160
Lin Zhixia's special training,

606
00:35:58,760 --> 00:35:59,800
that's something I can't take,

607
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:01,320
yet you persevered.

608
00:36:02,230 --> 00:36:04,510
The effort and hardship
you put into the competition,

609
00:36:04,510 --> 00:36:06,310
only you know best in your heart.

610
00:36:08,630 --> 00:36:11,630
You have been constantly
breaking through yourself.

611
00:36:11,880 --> 00:36:13,150
Don't you want to see

612
00:36:13,150 --> 00:36:14,680
where your limit really is?

613
00:36:15,920 --> 00:36:18,430
[Women]

614
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:38,800
Lin Zhixia.

615
00:36:39,280 --> 00:36:40,360
I think for the last modeling question,

616
00:36:40,360 --> 00:36:41,610
we can use Markov chains

617
00:36:41,610 --> 00:36:43,960
and binomial
and Poisson distribution models, right?

618
00:36:43,960 --> 00:36:44,760
I think this kind of question

619
00:36:44,760 --> 00:36:46,190
is most suitable to use probability rules

620
00:36:46,190 --> 00:36:47,390
as a modeling method.

621
00:36:47,760 --> 00:36:48,670
I have an idea.

622
00:36:49,030 --> 00:36:50,960
How about using Bayesian methods?

623
00:36:51,280 --> 00:36:52,400
I'm fine with anything.

624
00:36:52,400 --> 00:36:54,230
Jiang, what do you think?

625
00:36:56,510 --> 00:36:58,880
Our team has
the best average foundational ability.

626
00:36:58,880 --> 00:37:00,150
Our advantage is in the front end,

627
00:37:00,150 --> 00:37:01,460
that is, the establishment of the model

628
00:37:01,460 --> 00:37:03,230
and the parameter estimation stage.

629
00:37:03,230 --> 00:37:04,400
So Markov chains

630
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:06,440
and the binomial
and Poisson distribution methods

631
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:07,710
are the most secure for us.

632
00:37:07,710 --> 00:37:08,800
This model is classic

633
00:37:08,800 --> 00:37:09,960
and highly applicable.

634
00:37:09,960 --> 00:37:10,840
Other groups are highly likely

635
00:37:10,840 --> 00:37:12,670
to choose this problem-solving approach.

636
00:37:12,670 --> 00:37:13,630
Then what everyone is competing on

637
00:37:13,630 --> 00:37:15,110
is computational complexity.

638
00:37:15,110 --> 00:37:17,170
Our group has no absolute advantage.

639
00:37:17,400 --> 00:37:19,320
If Team 4 also chooses the same method,

640
00:37:19,320 --> 00:37:20,550
with Tang Tingting's personal ability

641
00:37:20,550 --> 00:37:21,590
and her condition today,

642
00:37:21,590 --> 00:37:23,030
she will definitely not be as good as us

643
00:37:23,030 --> 00:37:24,360
in terms of details and rigor.

644
00:37:24,360 --> 00:37:25,320
So I think

645
00:37:25,840 --> 00:37:27,440
Lin Zhixia won't choose this.

646
00:37:27,440 --> 00:37:29,840
She is too confident
in her personal abilities.

647
00:37:29,840 --> 00:37:31,030
So she is very likely to choose

648
00:37:31,030 --> 00:37:33,550
a modeling method
that emphasizes her personal thinking.

649
00:37:33,550 --> 00:37:36,150
Such as grey models
and Grey Relation Analysis.

650
00:37:36,150 --> 00:37:37,960
To widen the gap with other groups,

651
00:37:37,960 --> 00:37:39,710
I think it is more appropriate
to use grey models

652
00:37:39,710 --> 00:37:41,590
and Grey Relation Analysis now.

653
00:37:41,710 --> 00:37:43,320
It can show strategic insights

654
00:37:43,320 --> 00:37:45,280
that probability models cannot provide,

655
00:37:45,280 --> 00:37:47,110
and can still work

656
00:37:47,150 --> 00:37:48,280
when data is scarce.

657
00:37:48,670 --> 00:37:50,870
This method is more flexible and agile.

658
00:37:51,110 --> 00:37:53,510
But even if it's completed
by Lin Zhixia alone,

659
00:37:53,510 --> 00:37:56,190
it won't affect
their team's final presentation.

660
00:37:56,190 --> 00:37:57,550
What if the result is better?

661
00:37:57,550 --> 00:37:58,230
No.

662
00:37:59,070 --> 00:38:01,760
Although she has a deep understanding
of mathematical principles,

663
00:38:01,760 --> 00:38:03,760
she will definitely forget the fact

664
00:38:05,840 --> 00:38:07,590
that this is a team competition.

665
00:38:07,590 --> 00:38:08,550
But in this way,

666
00:38:08,590 --> 00:38:10,280
it relies on
your personal systems thinking

667
00:38:10,280 --> 00:38:11,440
and interpretation ability.

668
00:38:11,440 --> 00:38:13,150
Is there anything else I can do?

669
00:38:13,150 --> 00:38:14,590
Leave it to me, don't worry.

670
00:38:14,590 --> 00:38:16,190
There won't be any problems.

671
00:38:27,360 --> 00:38:28,190
Frankly speaking,

672
00:38:28,190 --> 00:38:30,880
the theoretical model
of Team 4 is very perfect,

673
00:38:31,230 --> 00:38:32,630
but there are 2 problems.

674
00:38:33,920 --> 00:38:34,710
First,

675
00:38:34,570 --> 00:38:37,260
[Judge]

676
00:38:34,800 --> 00:38:38,000
the assumptions
in the modeling process are not perfect.

677
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:40,550
Of course,
the final result won't be affected,

678
00:38:40,550 --> 00:38:42,350
but it misses the scoring point.

679
00:38:42,800 --> 00:38:44,110
But if you

680
00:38:44,110 --> 00:38:45,030
analyze the above factors

681
00:38:45,030 --> 00:38:48,280
using binomial
and Poisson distributions here,

682
00:38:47,310 --> 00:38:49,910
[Judges]

683
00:38:48,480 --> 00:38:49,880
wouldn't it be better?

684
00:38:51,960 --> 00:38:54,320
In addition, grey models

685
00:38:54,320 --> 00:38:57,670
is actually a prediction model
built by fitting

686
00:38:57,670 --> 00:39:00,000
the original data
with an exponential function.

687
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:01,110
When the data doesn't

688
00:39:01,110 --> 00:39:03,000
have good smoothness,

689
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:04,800
it will produce certain errors.

690
00:39:04,840 --> 00:39:06,070
So this

691
00:39:06,070 --> 00:39:07,510
is very obviously

692
00:39:07,880 --> 00:39:10,880
a complete model thought up by one person.

693
00:39:10,960 --> 00:39:12,480
Which one of you is it?

694
00:39:17,070 --> 00:39:18,440
What this question tests

695
00:39:18,440 --> 00:39:20,670
is not entirely about right or wrong,

696
00:39:20,690 --> 00:39:22,710
[Judges]

697
00:39:20,760 --> 00:39:22,800
but more importantly, teamwork.

698
00:39:23,190 --> 00:39:24,230
A beautiful theory,

699
00:39:24,230 --> 00:39:26,400
combined with perfect data insight,

700
00:39:26,400 --> 00:39:27,710
can get a full score.

701
00:39:27,920 --> 00:39:30,360
I will award this contest's MVP

702
00:39:30,360 --> 00:39:32,400
to this student.

703
00:39:32,430 --> 00:39:34,550
Her model is impeccable.

704
00:39:34,670 --> 00:39:35,480
However,

705
00:39:35,480 --> 00:39:38,320
just looking at the focal point
of the last question,

706
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:40,840
I think Team 2's plan

707
00:39:40,840 --> 00:39:42,360
is more balanced.

708
00:39:43,070 --> 00:39:46,150
So I want to give Team 2 full marks.

709
00:39:47,150 --> 00:39:48,110
Team 4...

710
00:39:49,610 --> 00:39:53,790
[Judges]

711
00:39:50,150 --> 00:39:51,150
It's 20 points.

712
00:39:53,930 --> 00:39:57,480
[1st Place,
Nanhai No. 1 High School Team 2]

713
00:39:56,320 --> 00:39:58,670
Congratulations to Team 2
for winning the contest.

714
00:39:58,670 --> 00:39:59,360
We won!

715
00:39:59,880 --> 00:40:00,480
Did we win?

716
00:40:00,710 --> 00:40:01,400
-We're the champions!
-Quick!

717
00:40:01,400 --> 00:40:02,070
We won.

718
00:40:29,740 --> 00:40:33,290
[1st Place,
Nanhai No. 1 High School Team 2]

719
00:40:33,290 --> 00:40:36,290
[2nd Place,
Nanhai No. 1 High School Team 4]

720
00:41:25,010 --> 00:41:25,740
You're back.

721
00:41:26,150 --> 00:41:28,550
Just in time.
Wash your hands and let's eat.

722
00:41:30,800 --> 00:41:32,590
I'm not hungry, I won't eat.

723
00:41:43,110 --> 00:41:44,320
This is so sumptuous.

724
00:41:45,880 --> 00:41:46,440
Come on.

725
00:41:46,440 --> 00:41:47,800
It's all your favorite.

726
00:41:48,150 --> 00:41:49,610
Medium rare.

727
00:41:52,230 --> 00:41:53,630
Double cheese.

728
00:41:54,630 --> 00:41:56,320
Hurry, while it's hot.

729
00:42:00,800 --> 00:42:01,630
Whenever we eat Western food,

730
00:42:01,630 --> 00:42:03,480
I always think of
how you looked when you were little.

731
00:42:03,480 --> 00:42:04,630
So cute.

732
00:42:05,030 --> 00:42:07,400
Do you remember
the first time you ate Western food?

733
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:08,530
You said to me, "Mom,

734
00:42:09,150 --> 00:42:11,750
this is the most delicious thing
in the world."

735
00:42:12,670 --> 00:42:13,930
Yang from my workplace

736
00:42:14,030 --> 00:42:15,760
insisted on buying you snacks.

737
00:42:15,840 --> 00:42:17,110
When he asked what you liked,

738
00:42:17,110 --> 00:42:19,360
you told him you liked Western food.

739
00:42:20,150 --> 00:42:21,590
You wanted T-bone steak,

740
00:42:21,760 --> 00:42:23,220
Nasi Goreng, and borscht.

741
00:42:23,420 --> 00:42:25,320
You completely confused him.

742
00:42:26,280 --> 00:42:28,540
In the end,
he bought you to Western food.

743
00:42:36,190 --> 00:42:38,400
Look at me!

744
00:42:38,440 --> 00:42:39,280
Your dad

745
00:42:39,880 --> 00:42:42,000
insisted we call him before eating.

746
00:42:42,000 --> 00:42:43,670
He said you haven't called him for days,

747
00:42:43,670 --> 00:42:44,800
and he misses you.

748
00:42:45,320 --> 00:42:45,960
Mom.

749
00:42:47,360 --> 00:42:49,560
Why don't you mention the competition?

750
00:42:51,110 --> 00:42:52,030
Isn't it more obvious

751
00:42:52,030 --> 00:42:53,830
when you deliberately avoid it?

752
00:42:55,590 --> 00:42:57,670
I... I didn't.

753
00:42:57,670 --> 00:42:58,590
I know.

754
00:42:58,710 --> 00:43:01,360
You don't mention it
because you're afraid I'll be sad.

755
00:43:01,360 --> 00:43:02,710
I didn't get
a single question right today.

756
00:43:02,710 --> 00:43:04,070
I embarrassed you again, right?

757
00:43:04,070 --> 00:43:05,110
You might as well just

758
00:43:05,110 --> 00:43:06,840
scold me directly like before.

759
00:43:09,030 --> 00:43:10,550
Let's not talk about this for now.

760
00:43:10,550 --> 00:43:11,320
We are eating.

761
00:43:11,320 --> 00:43:13,450
-Fine. I apologize.
-Let’s eat first.

762
00:43:13,960 --> 00:43:14,840
I'm sorry.

763
00:43:16,360 --> 00:43:17,840
I know that by participating
in this math contest,

764
00:43:17,840 --> 00:43:19,570
I was just humiliating myself.

765
00:43:19,960 --> 00:43:21,000
I didn't want to go in the first place.

766
00:43:21,000 --> 00:43:22,550
You forced me to go.

767
00:43:23,150 --> 00:43:24,350
Have you given up now?

768
00:43:24,710 --> 00:43:25,920
Seeing your daughter is the dumbest one

769
00:43:25,920 --> 00:43:27,360
and the worst one

770
00:43:27,360 --> 00:43:28,920
among so many people—

771
00:43:29,000 --> 00:43:30,110
the one who always embarrasses you

772
00:43:30,110 --> 00:43:31,030
and isn't good enough—

773
00:43:31,030 --> 00:43:31,920
are you happy now?

774
00:43:31,920 --> 00:43:32,710
Tingting.

775
00:43:34,550 --> 00:43:35,760
Tingting. Hey...

776
00:43:37,920 --> 00:43:38,380
Waiter!

777
00:43:39,440 --> 00:43:40,210
Pack this up.

778
00:43:41,210 --> 00:43:42,610
Thank you. Please hurry.

779
00:43:53,510 --> 00:43:55,240
What's wrong with your sister?

780
00:43:57,510 --> 00:43:58,960
The provincial math contest.

781
00:43:58,960 --> 00:44:00,360
She didn't get 1st place.

782
00:44:03,000 --> 00:44:04,400
That's it?

783
00:44:04,400 --> 00:44:05,320
That scared me.

784
00:44:06,150 --> 00:44:08,350
Let's not talk about the contest today.

785
00:44:08,590 --> 00:44:09,840
If she doesn't want to eat,

786
00:44:09,840 --> 00:44:11,370
let her be alone for a while.

787
00:44:12,320 --> 00:44:12,820
Okay.

788
00:44:13,920 --> 00:44:15,960
Then go wash your hands and come eat.

789
00:44:32,690 --> 00:44:33,500
I thought

790
00:44:35,130 --> 00:44:36,380
being one step ahead

791
00:44:38,190 --> 00:44:40,590
could shield you from all the storms.

792
00:44:43,030 --> 00:44:44,030
Until my shadow

793
00:44:45,010 --> 00:44:46,810
completely blocked your light.

794
00:44:49,130 --> 00:44:49,940
I'm sorry.

795
00:44:50,800 --> 00:44:52,360
This apology

796
00:44:53,630 --> 00:44:56,560
cannot compare
to the height of your stacked drafts.

797
00:44:58,340 --> 00:44:59,670
My self-righteousness

798
00:45:00,530 --> 00:45:02,070
so easily shattered

799
00:45:02,900 --> 00:45:04,210
everyone's hard work.

800
00:45:07,670 --> 00:45:08,840
I don't deserve us.

801
00:45:10,670 --> 00:45:11,920
And I definitely don't deserve first place.
